Two new engine facts worth knowing beyond the prior findings: rule bodies see every `:in` source (leading `$sym` pattern selector), and — the sharpest trap — a bare non-`?` symbol in a pattern is a binding lookup that acts as a **wildcard** when unbound (`[?v :variable x]` silently matches all variables). My first premise check hit this; fixed with a scalar `:in` input.

